Kibana

# Install Kibana

sudo apt install kibana -y

# Edit Kibana configuration
		

Configuration:

server.host: "0.0.0.0"
server.port: 5601
elasticsearch.hosts: ["http://localhost:9200"]

Start Kibana:
sudo systemctl enable --now kibana && sudo systemctl status kibana


 Kibana enrollment token generate

sudo /usr/share/elasticsearch/bin/elasticsearch-create-enrollment-token -s kibana


Password RESET

sudo /usr/share/elasticsearch/bin/elasticsearch-reset-password -u elastic -i


Kibana verification code

sudo /usr/share/kibana/bin/kibana-verification-code


Access:
http://<SERVER-IP>:5601




Filebeat

# Install Filebeat

sudo apt install filebeat -y

# Check Filebeat

sudo systemctl status filebeat


Configure Elasticsearch output:

sudo nano /etc/filebeat/filebeat.yml

Example:

output.elasticsearch:
  hosts: ["http://localhost:9200"]
  username: "elastic"
  password: "YOUR_ELASTIC_PASSWORD"
  ssl.verification_mode: none

Disable Logstash output if present:
#output.logstash:
#  hosts: ["localhost:5044"]



5. Enable Nginx/Apache module example
sudo filebeat modules enable nginx

sudo filebeat modules list

Configure module:

sudo nano /etc/filebeat/modules.d/nginx.yml


Then:
sudo filebeat setup -e



6. Start Filebeat

sudo systemctl enable --now filebeat && sudo systemctl status filebeat


Test:

sudo filebeat test config
sudo filebeat test output


7. Verify everything

sudo systemctl status elasticsearch kibana filebeat
curl -k https://localhost:9200
curl http://localhost:5601

Flow to remember for interviews:

Application/Server Logs → Filebeat → Elasticsearch → Kibana → Visualization




